  "body": "## Summary\n\nDocument the next eight unticked items from #3909. This is partial umbrella coverage. The remaining checklist stays open.\n\n| Item | Guide section | Coverage |\n|---|---|---|\n| #3833 | `operations/operations-2d.md` — 2D Contour | Outside ramp entry, Helix substitution, tabs, short paths and compensation limits. |\n| #3861 | `automate/cli.md` — Control a running window | `--ui call`, `mcp`, `windows`, selection, shared undo and refusal exits. |\n| #3900 | `set-up/tools.md` — Create and edit a tool; First run | Separate tool window, Document/Catalog sources and removal of the dock tab. |\n| #3903 | `set-up/tools.md` — Create and edit a tool | Tool/Details editor, Apply, tool rail and independent drafts. |\n| #3496 | `multi-axis/operations-multiaxis.md` — Rotary Offset | Zigzag closing rings without duplicate seam cuts. |\n| #3516 | `operations/operations-2d.md` — 2D Pocket | Protected picks, full-tool clearance, rest machining and MCP setter. |\n| #3579 | `operations/operations-2d.md` — 2D Pocket | Missed-relief note, boundary corner coordinates and remaining material. |\n| #3762 | `reference/troubleshooting.md` — GPU compute falls back to the CPU | First fault, retained CPU path, compute switch and rendering limits. |\n\nPaths above are under `site/content/guide/`. The decision record lists the merged source PRs.\n\n## Readings and scope\n\nI checked all eight merged PR descriptions and their current implementation on upstream main `72890060b53a6dc836e8cee1d928226e11a4d753`.\nThe guide still omitted these changes. The new tests failed before the prose changes and pass afterward.\nThe current tool editor also has a Recipes tab. The prose does not limit it to two tabs.\nThe CLI syntax block is not captured output. The older headless captures remain identified as 0.18.0 output.\n\nNo CAM code, generated programs, machine files, examples, fixtures, screenshot goldens, shared changelog or process files change.\nNo new screenshot is needed for these prose-only changes. Existing operation pictures remain illustrations.\nThe separate MCP page is unchanged. The other open 2D-guide contributions change Chamfer and Bore, not these Contour/Pocket paragraphs.\n\n## Verification\n\nWith release-pinned Zola 0.23.6:\n\n- Eight new coverage pins: pass. Each failed on the unchanged guide before implementation.\n- Focused site gate: **65 tests pass**, exit 0. Command from `site/tests`:\n  `ZOLA=<zola-0.23.6> python3 -m unittest -v test_release_027_batch3 test_guide_navigation test_guide_after_1995 test_guide_refresh test_operation_reference test_release_026_gaps test_release_026_guide test_release_022_guide test_guide_images`.\n- Guide navigation, deployment-prefix links and HTML anchors: pass. These are included in that focused gate.\n- `python3 -m unittest discover -s site/tests -v`: 112 tests, three failures. The unchanged base has the same three failures across 104 tests: two icon-byte mismatches (`op-rotary-contour`, `op-rotary-parallel`) and the missing `manualToolChange` manifest row. No new failure remains.\n- `zola --root site build`: pass.\n- `git diff --check`: pass.\n- `CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=3 CAMCRAFT_GATE_SWEEP=off cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: exits 0 with **zero applicable Rust steps**. This is not the documentation verification; the site tests above ran.\n\nNot run: Rust application, UI, catalog, light, heavy and release lanes; interactive CAM or machine trials. No application code changes.\nNo CI pass is claimed. The current branch-rules and ruleset queries return no required checks. The branch response lists empty required-status contexts and checks.\n\nChangelog: none\nEffort: medium\nProcess change: no\n\nRefs #3909\n",
